          "content": "A Square and A Cube"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.849,
            0.164
          ],
          "content": "Thus, we can say that a natural number is not a perfect square if it cannot be expressed as a sum of successive odd natural numbers starting from 1. We can use this result to find out whether a natural number is a perfect square."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.173,
            0.846,
            0.213
          ],
          "content": "？ Find how many numbers lie between two consecutive perfect squares. Do you notice a pattern?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.22,
            0.848,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": "？ How many square numbers are there between 1 and 100? How many are between 101 and 200? Using the table of squares you filled earlier, enter the values below, tabulating the number of squares in each block of 100. What is the largest square less than 1000?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.194,
